From 65e010cecabf93c449209c19271a4a938815f55f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Eden PS4 <eden-ps4@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 14:33:48 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 69/70] dynarmic: one page table walk for A64 loads and stores
 that share a base (page table without fastmem)

A64 version of A32SharedWalkPass: loads and stores (8 to 128 bits, LDP/STP's 128-bit accesses
included; not acquire/release) through one base register value plus constants within a block,
spanning at most 256 bytes, share one walk (A64HostPointer at the first: the host address of the
span, or 0 when it crosses a page, is outside the address space, is unmapped, or is marked and one
of them writes). Each becomes A64ReadMemoryVia*/A64WriteMemoryVia*: a test, a branch and one host
load or store; when the shared walk failed, its own walk and then the same fallbacks as before.
The base is followed through chains of constant adds and subtracts, so a pre-indexed STP's new SP
and the stores after it, and the epilogue's loads, are one group.
(UserConfig::page_table_shared_walk, on by default.)

Host harness (Eden's page table configuration, a 32-bit space, block ids above 511): a call with
a prologue, an epilogue and seven struct accesses 27-28.5 ns -> 11.7-12.1 ns. 1,500 random A64
programs (every size, LDUR/STUR, signed loads, LDP/STP of W, X, D and Q with offsets, pre- and
post-index, register offsets, SIMD, prologues on SP, a load into its own base, a store of the base
itself; at page boundaries, on a marked page, next to and on an unmapped one, outside the address
space) give the same registers, vectors, SP and memory with and without it.
